  title={Design of Direct 48-V/1-V Three-Path Four-State Switching Power Converter With Adaptive VCF Rebalancing and Dual-Edge tdead Modulation},
  year={2024},
  volume={59},
  number={5},
  pages={1592-1602},
  abstract={This article presents a new power converter capable of direct 48-V/1-V dc–dc conversion with high efficiency. The proposed three-path four-state (3P4S) hybrid switching power stage enables high switching frequency ( $f_{\mathrm {SW}}$ ) operation and minimizes power passives by significantly reducing power switch voltage stress. To address the issues of power delivery path imbalances and potential device breakdown, an adaptive flying capacitor voltage ( $V_{\mathrm {CF}}$ ) rebalancing technique is introduced that improves design robustness and eliminates the need for direct floating  $V_{\mathrm {CF}}$  sensing. Additionally, a dual-edge deadtime ( $t_{\mathrm {dead}}$ ) modulation with elastic  $t_{\mathrm {dead}}$  control at switching nodes optimizes converter efficiency across different input voltage and load conditions. An IC prototype of the design was fabricated and tested with input voltage  $V_{\mathrm {IN}}$  ranging from 12 to 48 V, delivering up to 4 W of power at 1-V  $V_{\mathrm {O}}$ . It achieves peak efficiency of 90.7% and 85.6% for 12-V/1-V and 48-V/1-V power conversion, respectively, at an effective switching frequency of 4.5 MHz, which is based on a three-phase operation with each phase at 1.5 MHz. The adaptive  $V_{\mathrm {CF}}$  rebalancing technique reduces  $V_{\mathrm {CF}}$  imbalance error by up to 65.1%. Overall, the proposed 3P4S hybrid switching power converter offers an efficient and robust solution for direct dc–dc conversion with a wide  $V_{\mathrm {IN}}$  range.},
  keywords={Switches;Topology;Inductors;Discharges (electric);Capacitors;Switching circuits;Stress;Adaptive VCF rebalancing technique;direct 48-V/1-V dc-dc conversion;dual-edge tdead modulation;hybrid switching converter;three-path four-state (3P4S) power stage},
